# Ported-From: danwright32/downbeat .gitignore @ 563865a7e8a93c678e6eed38c86281c8d9a730d0
#
# Every entry carries its reason. An entry with no reason, sitting beside
# neighbours that have one, is evidence nobody reasoned about it (L233).
#
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC for the whole build (Dan's decision, 2026-09-05, on
# Actions minutes: unlimited on a public repo, 2,000 minutes a month on a private
# one, and macOS runners bill at ten times the rate). So this file is the only
# thing between a real receipt and a public URL, and ovation#15 covers making it
# private at the end.
#
# `.gitignore` alone is NOT the whole guard, and cannot be: an entry added AFTER
# a file was committed hides it from `git status` while leaving it in every clone
# for ever. scripts/check-custody-not-staged.sh answers that question, runs in
# the pre push hook, and is seen to fail on exactly that shape.

# macOS writes these into every directory it displays.
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Xcode build products and per user state.
build/
DerivedData/
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
*.xccheckout
*.moved-aside
*.xcscmblueprint

# GENERATED by XcodeGen from project.yml, which is the source of truth.
# Committing it would give the repository two descriptions of one project that
# drift silently, and the generated one is what Xcode actually reads (L41).
# This is a deliberate DIFFERENCE from the port source, which commits its project.
Ovation.xcodeproj/

# Swift Package Manager working directories.
.build/
.swiftpm/
Packages/
Package.pins

# Editor scratch.
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# CUSTODY. Dan's real receipts, for the 4a and 4b reader measurements. The PATH
# is machine local and the samples are never in this repository (L155). They
# carry vendor names, amounts and dates from real purchases.
.receipt-samples

# CUSTODY. The real QuickBooks exports for the Phase 3 import. They carry client
# names, invoice numbers and amounts for every job of 2026.
.quickbooks-samples

# DELIBERATELY NOT PORTED, recorded so its absence is a decision rather than an
# oversight: the source ignores `.reserved-names`, a machine local list of real
# show titles that its identity guard reads. Ovation's guard DERIVES its needles
# from the live export, the custody snapshots and its own store instead, which is
# the correction L217 made after that design reported `noList`, examined nothing,
# and left a real venue name sitting in four test files. Ovation has no such file
# and must not grow one: a guard whose needles come from a list somebody has to
# maintain is a guard that goes blind when the list is missing (ovation#5).

# Python bytecode. scripts/check-identity-leaks.sh is a Python program, and
# scripts/test-output-privacy.sh imports it as a module to reuse its needle
# derivation rather than keeping a second copy. That import used to leave a
# __pycache__ directory in scripts/. The suite now runs python with -B so none
# is written at all, and this entry is the second line of defence rather than
# the fix: an ignored artifact is still an artifact somebody's guard has to walk.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Playwright MCP writes snapshots and screenshots here. Anchored with a
# leading slash so it matches only the repo root, never a same named
# directory anywhere else in the tree.
/.playwright-mcp/
